 "conventions": {
  "units": "metres, glTF Y-up, origin at the base centre (y=0 on the ground/waterline); scale per instance for size variety (height is the unscaled asset height)",
  "materials": "material name prefix = role: leaf_* / flower_* = alpha cards (use flora leafMaterial(map) with map.userData.normalMap = normalMap); wood_* = trunk/stipe/stems (opaque, textured, single-sided); solid_* = opaque leaves modelled as geometry (double-sided, textured); body_* = fauna (opaque)",
  "attribute": "_FLORA (vec2, GLTFLoader exposes it as geometry.attributes._flora): x = wind sway weight 0 base -> 1 tips, y = exposure/AO 0 inside -> 1 outer shell; same semantics as GeoBuilder flora. geometry.setAttribute(\"flora\", geometry.attributes._flora)",
  "windAmp": "metres of sway at weight 1 (pass as leafMaterial amp / windPosition(amp) for ALL materials of the species so leaves and wood move together)",
  "lodDistances": "[lod0->lod1, lod1->impostor] metres from the camera route; fauna/solids without impostor: cull beyond the second value",
  "impostor": "3x3 atlas: colour 1024^2 (cellPx 341), normal 512^2 same layout. cells 0-7 = side views, camera at azimuth k*45deg about +Y starting at +Z (camera on +Z looking toward -Z), increasing toward +X; cell 8 = top. Row 0 of the image = cells 0,1,2. Colour = unlit albedo x baked exposure (sRGB) + alpha; normal = object-space normal*0.5+0.5 (linear). Quad width x height metres, bottom edge at y=bottom. aninga/caete/bromelia/fauna have none: cull beyond lodDistances[1]",
  "compression": "EXT_meshopt_compression (GLTFLoader.setMeshoptDecoder), WebP textures; normals/uvs quantized, positions float (quantized positions need a node dequant transform that breaks the metre-based wind and geometry extraction into InstancedMesh)",
  "fauna": "forward = +Z; static meshes (no rig)",
  "files": "each LOD = <id>_lodN.gltf + .bin + EXTERNAL .webp textures shared by both LODs (load with GLTFLoader as usual; the browser fetches each texture once). lods[i].files lists everything; species.bytes = all files of the species",
  "priority": "critical = load before first frame (palms, trees); optional = stream after first frame (bromelia, aninga, caete, jacare, garca)"
 },
